riscos-mesa: "mixed" test programs
==================================

These are some of the test programs linked the new way riscos-crossdev 1.11
allows: UnixLib (and libstdc++) are linked into each program as usual, but
OpenGL (OSMesa), EGL, GLU, SDL 2 and OpenAL are shared libraries in
!MesaLibs, which !SharedLibs loads when the program starts. Programs using
the same !MesaLibs share one copy of each library in memory, and each
program is much smaller (glbench: about 9 MB linked statically, about
0.5 MB mixed).

This is a test. The ordinary (static) test programs, in the tests
directory, are unchanged and need none of this.

What it needs:
- !SharedLibs with ld-riscos/so/2 (GCCSDK 8 or later; Iris includes one),
  in !Boot.Resources. riscos.info's SharedLibs 4.0 has only ld-riscos/so/1
  and won't run these. On RISC OS on Linux, NativeSupport 0.33 or later.
- SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later, and ARMEABISupport.
- !MesaLibs: there is a copy here, which the Obey files use if no
  !MesaLibs has been booted. For other programs, copy it to
  !Boot.Resources.

The Obey files (double-click):
  mx-glbench          glbench 640 480 5, results in ResultBench
  mx-glbench-game     its racing-game-like scene, results in ResultGame
  mx-egl-window       egltest in a window, results in eglwindow
  mx-gles-window      OpenGL ES 1.1 and 2.0 in a window, gles-window
  mx-sdl              sdlgltest: SDL with OpenGL, 640x480
  mx-sdl-fb-overlay   sdlfbtest through the overlay, results in SDLFBovl
  mx-glu              glutest (GLU), results in ResultGLU
  mx-al-tone          OpenAL's three tones, results in altone

What to compare, with the static programs run the same way:
- speed: glbench's times (the shared library is position-independent
  code, which was about 2% slower when tried in October);
- the pictures and sound: the same;
- memory: with two or three of them running at once, the free memory
  (Task Manager), against the same static programs.

If a program stops at once, a message from !SharedLibs or the program
says which library or module was missing.
